# Architecture: custom store, golden path

## Context

State is managed by a small in-house store in `app/src/store.ts`
(`createStore()` returning `{ getState, dispatch, subscribe }`). It is
deliberately NOT Redux, Zustand, MobX, or Jotai. The full architecture is
described in `materials/architecture-brief.md`.

## Rule

- All state changes MUST go through `store.dispatch(action)` — there is no
  other sanctioned way to change state.
- The golden path to add new behavior:
  1. Add a variant to the `Action` discriminated union in `app/src/types.ts`.
  2. Handle it in `app/src/reducer.ts`.
  3. Add an action creator in `app/src/actions.ts`.
  4. Add a colocated `*.test.ts`.
- UI/consumers call action creators from `app/src/actions.ts`; NEVER construct
  action objects by hand at the call site.
- Reads go through selectors in `app/src/selectors.ts` (`visibleTasks`,
  `remainingCount`), not by poking at `state.tasks` directly.
- NEVER add or suggest Redux, Zustand, MobX, Jotai, Recoil, or any other state
  library. Do not "modernize" the store engine.

## How to verify

1. `grep -rE "redux|zustand|mobx|jotai|recoil" app/src app/package.json` — zero matches.
2. Every new `Action` variant added in `types.ts` has a matching `case` in
   `reducer.ts` and a creator in `actions.ts`.
3. No file outside `store.ts` reassigns state; changes appear only as
   `dispatch(...)` calls.
